description: General engineering and code standards for the Resume Tailor AI app
alwaysApply: true
---

# General Rules

- Never break existing functionality.
- Write clean, production-ready code.
- Prefer reusable services over duplicated logic.
- Keep the project modular; keep frontend and backend responsibilities separate.
- Follow FastAPI best practices in `backend/`.

# AI/Prompt Code Rules

- Never hardcode prompts inline in service/route code. Keep all prompt text in
  `backend/app/prompts/` and import it from there.
- Keep AI-calling logic in `backend/app/services/` (e.g. `ai_tailor.py`), never
  inside `backend/app/api/routes/`. Routes only orchestrate services.
- Load all secrets (e.g. `OPENAI_API_KEY`) via `backend/app/core/config.py`
  (env vars). Never hardcode or log API keys.
- When a prompt needs to change, edit the dedicated prompt file — do not
  duplicate prompt text across multiple places.
- Write scalable, production-quality code; avoid one-off scripts in `app/`.
